28
00:01:57,555 --> 00:02:00,975
Ask a question, and it answers from your own notes, out loud.

29
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:05,520
🎤 “Explain my notes in simple words.”

30
00:02:12,082 --> 00:02:15,072
Like the answer? Say, add that to my notes.

31
00:02:18,091 --> 00:02:19,441
🎤 “Add that to my notes.”

32
00:02:25,767 --> 00:02:28,447
Time to revise? Just say, quiz me.

33
00:02:30,647 --> 00:02:32,097
🎤 “Quiz me on this notebook.”

34
00:02:35,784 --> 00:02:37,794
Want flashcards? Just ask.

35
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:41,154
🎤 “Make flashcards.”

36
00:02:46,895 --> 00:02:48,825
And it tells you what your notes are still missing.

37
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,020
🎤 “What did I miss?”

38
00:02:56,872 --> 00:02:59,372
In class? Say, record the lecture.

39
00:03:01,416 --> 00:03:02,716
🎤 “Record the lecture.”

40
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:20,200
🎓 Good morning everyone. Today, the Calvin cycle. In the stroma, the enzyme RuBisCO fixes carbon dioxide, and the ATP and NADPH from the light reactions turn it into glucose.

41
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,130
It captions the lecture live, then turns it into organised notes.

42
00:03:26,502 --> 00:03:29,072
No typing. No menus. Just your voice.

43
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:33,230
Notebook Companion. Think with your notes.
